# Shared form controls

Before adding a button, icon button, text field, select, textarea, date picker, or time field, read `frontend/src/ui` and use the shared component. Do not add a raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, or `<textarea>` with one-off classes for those jobs.

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Button | `ui/Button` — `variant`: `primary`, `secondary`, `danger`, `ghost`. `pressed` for a toggle. `icon` is a Lucide icon before the label |
| Icon-only button | `ui/IconButton` — `label` is the accessible name |
| Label, error, hint | `ui/Field` |
| Text, number, checkbox, color | `ui/Input` |
| Select | `ui/Select` |
| Multiline text | `ui/Textarea` |
| One civil day (`YYYY-MM-DD`) | `ui/DatePicker` |
| Inclusive civil-day range | `ui/DateRangeField` |
| One day plus a clock range | `ui/DateTimeRangeField` — calendar is a date range; clocks sit on the first and last day |
| Clock time (`HH:mm`) | `ui/TimeField` |
| Dialog | `ui/Modal` |
| Spinner | `ui/Spinner` |

`size` is `sm` (32px), `md` (44px, default), or `lg` (48px). Per breakpoint: `{ base: 'sm', md: 'md' }`. Dialog footer actions use `dialogButtonSize` from `ui/controlSize`.

`Input` draws the icon for email, search, and a show/hide control for password. `DatePicker` and `DateRangeField` draw a calendar. `DateTimeRangeField` draws a calendar with a clock. `TimeField` draws a clock. `Select` draws a chevron. Do not add a second icon for those. A native `datetime-local` input is not a date or time control.

If a control needs a new variant, extend the shared component. A raw element is for UI that is not in this list: calendar cells, chips, color swatches, menu rows.
